…stanceLock


fixes https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/issues/12345



When a second instance is created that is immediately closed, the `electron.launch` function now throws a canceled error. 
Both browser windows are then available on `firstApp.windows()`:


```js
const firstApp = await playwright._electron.launch({
  args: [path.join(__dirname, "electron-multi-window-app.js")],
});
try {
  await playwright._electron.launch({
    args: [path.join(__dirname, "electron-multi-window-app.js")],
  });
} catch (error) {
  if (error.message !== "electron.launch: canceled") {
    throw error;
  }
}
await firstApp.waitForEvent("window");
expect(firstApp.windows()).toHaveLength(2);
await firstApp.close();
```

