review_comments:
This test will be flaky / failing because `window` will be sometimes dispatched before `launch` completes. You should do something like this instead:

```js
  await Promise.all([
    firstApp.waitForEvent('window'),
    playwright._electron.launch({
      args: [path.join(__dirname, 'electron-multi-window-app.js')],
    })
  ]);
```

which reads is 'expect launching second instance of app to create a window in the first instance'.

Hm, Promise.all rejects as soon as  `playwright._electron.launch` rejects. 

![test-error](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23744935/159761314-bdf5a072-86e4-4d8d-838c-52e0fecb029e.png)

But I like the idea. What do you think about this version instead?

```js
const secondWindowPromise = firstApp.waitForEvent('window')
try {
  await playwright._electron.launch({
      args: [path.join(__dirname, 'electron-multi-window-app.js')],
    })
} catch (error) {
  if (error.message !== 'electron.launch: canceled') throw error;
}
await secondWindowPromise
expect(firstApp.windows()).toHaveLength(2);
```
